From: REIMU A/B <reimu@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_mass_storage: CD-ROM images bigger than 2.2 GiB

fsg_lun_open() cuts a CD-ROM image to 256*60*75 - 1 blocks (the most a CD's
MSF addresses reach), so a DVD-sized installer ISO (Windows, most Linux
distributions: 4-6 GiB) shows only its first 2.2 GiB to the host, and
whatever lies beyond reads as the end of the medium. Hosts read by LBA
(READ(10), 32-bit block numbers); only an MSF address in READ TOC can't hold
more, so that one saturates instead, and the image is cut only at 2^32 blocks.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/storage_common.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/storage_common.c
@@ -244,12 +244,14 @@
 	min_sectors = 1;
 	if (curlun->cdrom) {
 		min_sectors = 300;	/* Smallest track is 300 frames */
-		if (num_sectors >= 256*60*75) {
-			num_sectors = 256*60*75 - 1;
-			LINFO(curlun, "file too big: %s\n", filename);
-			LINFO(curlun, "using only first %d blocks\n",
-					(int) num_sectors);
-		}
+		/*
+		 * No cap at 256*60*75 blocks (a CD's MSF addressing, 2.2 GiB):
+		 * DVD and BD images are bigger, and hosts read by LBA (READ(10)
+		 * with 32-bit block numbers). Only an MSF address in the TOC
+		 * can't hold more: store_cdrom_address() saturates it.
+		 */
+		if (num_sectors > 0xffffffffLL)
+			num_sectors = 0xffffffffLL;
 	}
 	if (num_sectors < min_sectors) {
 		LINFO(curlun, "file too small: %s\n", filename);
@@ -299,6 +301,8 @@
 		 * Convert to Minutes-Seconds-Frames.
 		 * Sector size is already set to 2048 bytes.
 		 */
+		if (addr >= 256*60*75 - 2*75)	/* past what MSF can hold */
+			addr = 256*60*75 - 2*75 - 1;
 		addr += 2*75;		/* Lead-in occupies 2 seconds */
 		dest[3] = addr % 75;	/* Frames */
 		addr /= 75;
